# Supabase — use CLI, not MCP

For this repository, **do not use Supabase MCP**. It is not working in this project environment.

## Required

- Use the **Supabase CLI** as the primary option for:
  - Live database inspection / querying
  - Schema inspection
  - Migrations (create, apply, push, status)
- Prefer local migration files under `supabase/migrations/` and CLI workflows (`supabase db …`, `supabase migration …`, linked project commands) over any MCP-based database tools.

## Do not

- Do **not** call Supabase MCP tools for database view, schema discovery, or migrations.
- Do **not** spend time diagnosing or retrying Supabase MCP auth/connection failures for routine DB work — switch to the CLI instead.

## Exceptions

Only consider Supabase MCP if the user explicitly insists on it after being told it is unreliable here; still prefer CLI when possible.
